<article class="env-remark" id="04XP">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04XP">Remark <span data-tag="04XP">10.2.3.20</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category, let $Q$ denote the collection of all quotient morphisms in $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, and let $M$ denote the collection of all monomorphisms in $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. Then $Q$ and $M$ are closed under isomorphism (see Corollary <a data-tag="04WU" href="/tag/04WU">10.2.2.12</a> and Example <a data-tag="06TT" href="/tag/06TT">8.5.1.17</a>), and $Q$ is left orthogonal to $M$ (Lemma <a data-tag="04XC" href="/tag/04XC">10.2.3.10</a>). It follows that $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ has images if and only if the pair $(Q,M)$ is a factorization system on $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ (Definition <a data-tag="04PD" href="/tag/04PD">9.6.8.1</a>). </p>
